## ---- Parallel NOR flash (U4 28F00AM29EW, 128 MB, BPI x16 configuration flash) ---- [board: read only]
## Lower 64 MB (FA25=0) holds the FPGA bitstream, upper 64 MB (FA25=1) is system storage.
## FA25 is pulled low on the board by 330 ohm; per manual sec 2.4 the design should drive FA25_PU
## high after configuration so user logic cannot touch the configuration half.
## RS0/RS1 reach U4.1/U4.56 (same flash pins as FA23/FA24) through the optional SW12.
## A design that does not use the flash drives FCS_B, FOE_B and FWE_B high and leaves the rest
## alone: that is what every design here did. The flash was read whole with FWE_B tied high and
## FDQ as inputs; nothing here ever wrote it. F_BUSY_B is on the FPGA's own A25 pin (E20).
#set_property -dict { PACKAGE_PIN C23  IOSTANDARD LVCMOS33    } [get_ports { FCS_B }]              ; # bank 14, U4.32
