## ---- DDR3 SDRAM (2x PieceMakers PMF512816BBR-MBDN, 4 Gbit x16 each: 32-bit, 1 GiB) ---- [board, through MIG]
## Banks 32 (data) / 33 (address, control), VCCO 1.5V. These lines are for reference: with MIG in
## the design, its own XDC places and types every one of these pins (SSTL15_T_DCI on DQ,
## DIFF_SSTL15_T_DCI on DQS, SSTL15 on the rest, DIFF_SSTL15 on CK, LVCMOS15 on the reset), and
## mig/ here writes MIG's project from pins.csv. Plain SSTL15 is what is written below.
## Bank 33 has the DCI reference resistors (U9 VRN, V12 VRP); bank 32, which has the data, lists
## none, and MIG does not write this line itself. It is needed, and with it DCI matches on the board:
#set_property DCI_CASCADE {32} [get_iobanks 33]
## AE16 and Y18 (bank 32 VREF) are tied to V_VTT_0V75: external VREF.
